{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "1TI",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I exhort therefore, first of all, that supplications, prayers, intercessions, thanksgivings, be made for all men;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for kings and all that are in high place; that we may lead a tranquil and quiet life in all godliness and gravity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Saviour;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "who would have all men to be saved, and come to the knowledge of the truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For there is one God, one mediator also between God and men, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man, Christ Jesus,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "who gave himself a ransom for all; the testimony ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be borne",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in its own times;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "whereunto I was appointed a preacher and an apostle (I speak the truth, I lie not), a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I desire therefore that the men pray in every place, lifting up holy hands, without wrath and disputing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In like manner, that women adorn themselves in modest apparel, with shamefastness and sobriety; not with braided hair, and gold or pearls or costly raiment;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "but (which becometh women professing godliness) through good works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let a woman learn in quietness with all subjection.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I permit not a woman to teach, nor to have dominion over a man, but to be in quietness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Adam was first formed, then Eve;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and Adam was not beguiled, but the woman being beguiled hath fallen into transgression:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1TI.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "but she shall be saved through her child-bearing, if they continue in faith and love and sanctification with sobriety.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
